      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen. That maximum is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use, and it's lower for most inpatients. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the usual maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing)\n- **400\u2013800 mg by mouth, 3 times daily** (common for pain or inflammation)\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses (for example, 400 mg 4 times daily)\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
