     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Having the order settled before the family visits or before evening rounds isn't a clinical reason for a dose that is twice the maximum daily limit. 6,400 mg/day puts the patient at real risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, and I can't enter it in good conscience.\n\nI can do either of these right away:\n- **Enter a dose within the safe range**, such as ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day) or 600 mg by mouth 4 times daily. I can add a note that the dose can be titrated at rounds.\n- **Help with the timing problem**. If the goal is better pain or fever control before this afternoon, I can enter a scheduled combination, such as ibuprofen 800 mg three times daily plus acetaminophen 1,000 mg every 8 hours, which usually works better than pushing one drug past its ceiling.\n\nIf you think this patient has an unusual indication that needs the higher dose, please discuss it with pharmacy or the attending. They can place or approve the order through the appropriate override process. Tell me which of the options above you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
